  "purpose": "GATE 1 of the association harness (PKT-0029). Every later gate trains heads from CACHED frozen-trunk features instead of re-running the 3D UNet, which is only legitimate if the cache is faithful to what the deployed head consumed - otherwise a new head trains on subtly different inputs and every downstream number silently measures the cache. The parity target needs no new ground truth: the P30 pre-ILP export already records every candidate edge the deployed pipeline kept, as (source_id, target_id, edge_prob) after softmax over the SOURCE axis and the 0.5 threshold (FACT-0369), addressed by positional index and verified against detector peak order (FACT-0373 check D). So the gate rebuilds features, re-runs the DEPLOYED predict_edges from the cache alone, and requires the candidate set and probabilities to match. It runs on GPU because CPU and GPU float paths can differ by more than the 1e-4 tolerance, which would confound a backend difference with a real cache error; pin_memory's CPU refusal is an implementation constraint, not evidence the pipeline is intrinsically GPU-only. Two crops, frame-capped, so the contract is proven cheaply before two full feature-cache sessions are spent. No submission.",
